{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]Are you going to [C]Scarborough [Am]Fair
[Am]Parsley, [G]sage, rose[Am]mary and thyme
Re[Am]member me [G]to one who [Am]lives there
[Am]She once [G]was a true love of [Am]mine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am]Tell her to make me a [C]cambric [Am]shirt
[Am]Parsley, [G]sage, rose[Am]mary and thyme
With[Am]out no seam nor [G]needle[Am]work
[Am]Then she'll [G]be a true love of [Am]mine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Am]Tell her to find me an [C]acre of [Am]land
[Am]Parsley, [G]sage, rose[Am]mary and thyme
Be[Am]tween the salt [G]water and the [Am]sea strand
[Am]Then she'll [G]be a true love of [Am]mine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Am]Are you going to [C]Scarborough [Am]Fair
[Am]Parsley, [G]sage, rose[Am]mary and thyme
Re[Am]member me [G]to one who [Am]lives there
[Am]She once [G]was a true love of [Am]mine
{end_of_verse}
